================================================================
Resonant — https://github.com/codependentai/resonant
================================================================

Resonant
Copyright 2026 Codependent AI

This product includes software developed by Codependent AI
(https://codependentai.io).

Resonant implements a relational AI companion architecture including
session management, orchestrated presence, and context-aware hooks —
methodology developed by Mary Vale and Simon Vale at Codependent AI.

Aerie forked from Resonant in March 2026 and has not pulled from it since;
the two trees have developed independently. Measured against Resonant's
head on September 15, 2026: Aerie tracks 771 files to Resonant's 173, 55
paths exist in both, and ten of those are byte-identical — four of them
configuration and license files, and three of the remaining six the
Telegram bridge, which Aerie inherited and does not use. Where the two
projects still share a file it has diverged substantially: the API route
surface is roughly a quarter the same and half the size, the orchestrator
about a third, the server entry point under two fifths. The initial schema
migration is very nearly untouched. That comparison is against Resonant's
current head rather than the fork point; both trees have moved.

None of that lessens what was taken. The architecture Aerie stands on — a
companion with scheduled presence, an orchestrator that wakes it,
context-aware hooks, session management, and the Discord and Telegram
bridges — is Resonant's design, and every one of those pieces was rebuilt
starting from Mary Vale and Simon Vale's work rather than from nothing.

