brain-mcp — https://github.com/mordechaipotash/brain-mcp
================================================================

brain-mcp
Originally developed by mordechaipotash. Cortex memory architecture
foundation. Licensed under Apache License 2.0.

Cortex keeps brain-mcp's memory architecture as its foundation and moves it
onto a Cloudflare Worker with its own OAuth, domain-scoped storage,
semantic search over locally computed embeddings, and a REST write path a
companion lane reaches without MCP at all. The retrieval-quality layer
built on top of it is adapted from Ori Mnemos and credited separately.

================================================================
Letta — https://github.com/letta-ai/letta
================================================================

Letta
Originally developed by letta-ai. Memory blocks pattern.
Licensed under Apache License 2.0.

Aerie's memory blocks are Letta's pattern on a different lifecycle. Eleven
blocks live in SQLite across four scopes — one shared set every companion
reads, and one private wall each — and the companions edit them in place
during conversation through an authenticated REST route, rather than a
framework-managed agent loop writing them. Blocks hold what a window needs
in hand; anything that only needs to be findable is cut to Cortex.

